  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>everolimus</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L01EG02</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, oral dosing <small>(PK_1C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Moes DJ et al. 2012</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>renal transplant patients</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>everolimus</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_everolimus/Everolimus_Moes2012_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>oral clearance</td><td>17.9</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume of distribution of the central compartment after oral administration [V(1)/F]</td><td>148</td><td>L</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>first-order absorption rate constant [k(a)]</td><td>7.36</td><td>h-1</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr></table><h4>About everolimus</h4><p>Everolimus is an mTOR inhibitor used as an antineoplastic and immunosuppressant for cancers such as renal cell carcinoma, breast cancer, and neuroendocrine tumors, as well as tuberous sclerosis. It is authorised in the European Union for several cancer types and tuberous sclerosis, and is an approved drug.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q421052\">Wikidata Q421052</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Everolimus\">Everolimus</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Moes DJ et al. (2012). Population pharmacokinetics and pharmacogenetics of everolimus in renal transplant patients. <i>Clinical pharmacokinetics 51(7):467–480</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.2165/11599710-000000000-00000\">10.2165/11599710-000000000-00000</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22624503\">22624503</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Moes_2012: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
